Research using open-source information on satellites has been used to validate the status of satellites. The sources are listed below for reproducibility. 

The criteria of dual-use satellites were as followed:
1) The satellite company has a contract with the military.
2) The satellite is owned and built by a private company, but operated by either the military or a security-related government agency.
3) The satellite company is collaborating with the military on space research.

In all cases, when certain satellites or satellite series are mentioned, only those are coded as dual-use, otherwise it is assumed that the private company 
does not restrict their cooperation to specific satellites. 

